*The best observed strategy was the one that kept **pushing hard in the direction of the current motion** and only reduced the thrust **after** the car had already acquired sufficient speed.*  
The new bang‑bang‑plus‑position‑based policy captures exactly that idea, eliminates the idle periods that caused the ‑99.9 failures, and should give the highest cumulative reward among all hand‑crafted rules tried so far.  

