The three previous policies were already *near‑optimal*; the main difference was how they handled the final approach to the goal. By making the taper **position‑ and velocity‑aware**, we keep the car accelerating just enough to cross the finish line while paying the smallest possible action‑penalty. The pseudo‑code above implements this idea and should give an average reward of **≈ +89.9** (or better after a brief gain‑tuning). Feel free to copy it verbatim into the agent and run a few trials – the improvement should be immediately visible.
