|---------|------------|
| **Full‑throttle right** (`position < -0.30 → +1`) | Guarantees enough kinetic energy to climb the left hill – the biggest hurdle. |
| **Immediate left brake** (`velocity < -0.001 → -1`) | Prevents the car from drifting back left once it has overshot the goal. |
| **Three‑zone PD gains** | Gives a strong pull when far from the goal (`kp=0.5`) and a much tighter controller when close (`kp=3.0`). |
| **Scale ≥ 0.5** | Ensures the controller never starves for force when the car is already moving fast. |
| **Brake zone (0.38 ≤ position < 0.45)** | Adds a small left‑ward bias that linearly cancels the remaining right‑ward momentum, eliminating the last few negative‑reward steps. |
| **Dead‑band at the goal** (`abs(velocity) < 0.02`) | Once the car is essentially stopped on the hill, we stop issuing any force, avoiding the “wiggle’’ that produced the –0.1·a² penalty. |

